UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Burlington, Vermont, OVR Technology develops hardware and software that add olfactory cues to interactive media. The company was founded by a team spanning industrial design, fragrance creation, neuroscience, and software engineering, though a founding year and ownership structure have not been publicly disclosed.

The Core model offers ten scent channels and a desktop form factor, while the Pro provides sixteen channels in a pocket‑sized unit.

The technology targets video‑game players and creators, with explicit support for PC and VR titles.

The company positions itself as a first mover in digital scent, emphasizing the difficulty of pioneering the category. Its stated differentiation rests on the integration of hardware, proprietary Scentware® cartridges, and a software layer that synchronizes scent release with real‑time game data.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hardware design and manufacturing of personal scent displays", "Scentware\u00ae cartridge formulation and production", "Software development kit for game integration", "Real\u2011time scent diffusion control (burst/continuous modes)", "Multi\u2011channel scent mixing (up to three channels)"], "industries": ["Video games", "Virtual reality", "Interactive entertainment", "Indie game development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combined hardware, Scentware\u00ae cartridges, and software for real\u2011time scent in games", "Two device tiers: desktop Core (10 channels) and portable Pro (16 channels)", "Multi\u2011channel scent mixing (up to three simultaneous)", "Sub\u2011second scent delivery (500\u20131,000 ms time\u2011to\u2011perception)", "Partnership program for indie game studios"], "facts_used": ["Location: Burlington, Vermont -> /", "Product: Omara Core and Omara Pro scent displays -> /", "Technology: hardware, Scentware\u00ae, software integration -> /", "Team composition: industrial design, fragrance designers, neuroscientists, software engineers -> /", "Target industries: video games, VR, indie studios -> /", "Differentiators: first mover in digital scent, multi-channel mixing, sub-second delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''ve combined Hardware, Scentware\u00ae, and Software to unlock scent, allowing players to smell their virtual worlds in real time.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ovr-technology' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='OXOS Medical, Inc. is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia. The company was founded in June 2016 as Micro C, LLC, later renamed OXOS Medical, Inc., by Evan M. Ruff, who serves as CEO, and Gregory P. Kolovich, MD, a reconstructive hand surgeon who became frustrated with traditional imaging processes while at Harvard Medical School. That frustration inspired the development of the Micro C, the world''s first portable Dynamic Digital Radiography device for orthopedic surgery.

OXOS designs and manufactures portable X-ray systems, including the original Micro C and the newer MC2, which received FDA 510(k) clearance (K252068) in 2024. The devices are built around a low-radiation profile while maintaining high image quality, and incorporate the AiLARA system, an automated technology that optimizes radiation dose according to the ALARA principle. A team of engineers, designers, and clinical advisors supports development and commercialization, with the MC2 now available in the United States.

The company targets orthopedics, pediatrics, and sports medicine, serving clinicians and medical practices nationwide. Testimonials cite use by hand and upper extremity surgeons, orthopaedic surgeons for professional sports teams (including the Jacksonville Jaguars), foot and ankle surgeons, and at off-road racing events through the non-profit Safety On Site. The portable systems are designed for point-of-care imaging in diverse clinical settings.

OXOS states its mission is to allow anyone, anywhere to access radiographic diagnostics at the point of need, expanding availability and changing how healthcare is delivered. The company emphasizes three pillars: safety through low radiation exposure, simplicity via portable and modular design, and intelligence through real-time diagnosis enabled by optimized alignment and a no-fire positioning system.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Portable X-ray system design and manufacturing", "Dynamic digital radiography", "FDA 510(k) regulatory clearance", "Automated radiation dose optimization (AiLARA)", "Point-of-care radiographic imaging", "Clinical user needs management", "Medical device commercialization"], "industries": ["Orthopedics", "Pediatrics", "Sports Medicine"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Micro C portable X-ray device", "MC2 portable X-ray device", "AiLARA radiation optimization system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA 510(k) cleared portable X-ray devices (Micro C and MC2)", "AiLARA automated radiation optimization system", "Low radiation dose with high image quality", "Portable, modular, easy-to-use design for point-of-care use", "Real-time diagnosis with optimized alignment and no-fire positioning"], "facts_used": ["Company name and HQ: Atlanta, Georgia -> db", "Founded June 2016 as Micro C, LLC, later OXOS Medical, Inc. -> /about", "Founders: Evan M. Ruff (CEO) and Gregory P. Kolovich, MD (CMO) -> /about", "Origin: Greg Kolovich frustrated with traditional imaging at Harvard Medical School -> /about", "Products: Micro C and MC2 portable X-ray devices -> /about, /", "FDA 510(k) clearances: Micro C (2021), AiLARA (2021), MC2 (2024, K252068) -> /about, /", "Mission: Allow anyone, anywhere to access radiographic diagnostics at point of need -> /about", "Differentiators: Safe (low radiation), Simple (portable/modular), Smart (real-time diagnosis, optimized alignment, no-fire positioning) -> /", "Industries served: Orthopedics, Pediatrics, Sports Medicine -> /", "Customer examples: Dr. Marc Tanner, Dr. Kevin Kaplan, Dr. Robert Santrock, Dr. Sunishka Wimalawansa -> /", "Team: engineers, designers, creators, executives -> /about", "Equipment: Micro C, MC2, AiLARA -> /about, /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Micro C, LLC., later named OXOS Medical, Inc., was founded in June to develop and commercialize the world''s first portable Dynamic Digital Radiography device for orthopedic surgery.", "founded_year": "2016", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='oxos-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
