UPDATE companies SET description='Old Dominion Furniture Co. operates from Lynchburg, Virginia, where it has served the hospitality market for over four decades. The company is led by presidents John Morgan and Laura Morgan, supported by a dedicated team including sales, freight, accounting, and shipping specialists. While the exact founding year is not publicly stated, the business emphasizes a legacy built on combining the personal touch of a small enterprise with the capacity of a larger operation.

The company manufactures a full range of contract furniture for commercial spaces, including table tops, chairs, booths, table bases, barstools, child seating, and custom pieces. Table tops are produced from regionally sourced lumber through a six-step finishing process that includes hand-wiped stain, a wash coat, oil-based filler, and three coats of conversion varnish with sanding between coats. Chairs and barstools are built on hardwood frames with premium finishes and high-density commercial-grade foam. Booths feature one-piece frame construction, web seating with high-density urethane foam, and heavy-duty textured plastic bases reinforced with corner protectors. All items are crafted and quality-checked at the firm''s Virginia facility before being shipped in a single delivery.

Old Dominion Furniture serves restaurants, country clubs, senior living communities, corporate offices, and educational institutions. The company collaborates directly with business owners, designers, and architects to develop furniture packages that align with specific design visions and budgets.

The firm positions itself as both a manufacturer and a design partner, highlighting its in-house craftsmen and a service model that blends personal attention with large-scale reliability. Its quality statement underscores control over every production step, from raw material to finished product, as the foundation for durability in high-traffic environments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and manufacturing", "Table top manufacturing with six-step finishing process", "Chair and barstool construction and upholstery", "Booth construction with one-piece frame and web seating", "In-house craftsmanship and quality control", "Direct shipping in one delivery", "Design consultation and furniture package development"], "industries": ["Restaurants", "Country Clubs", "Senior Living", "Corporate", "Education"], "materials": ["Regionally sourced lumber", "Hardwood frames", "Premium grade finishes", "High-density commercial grade foam", "Oil-based filler", "Conversion varnish", "Heavy duty textured plastic", "Corner protectors", "Web seating", "High-density urethane foam"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All furniture manufactured start-to-finish at their Virginia facility for total quality control", "Six-step hand-finished table top process with three coats of conversion varnish", "One-piece frame booth construction eliminates loose joints", "Web seating with high-density urethane foam retains shape for booth life", "In-house craftsmen build and inspect every piece before single-delivery shipment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lynchburg, Virginia -> db", "Over 40 years of experience -> /", "Presidents John Morgan and Laura Morgan -> /about-us", "Manufactures table tops, chairs, booths, table bases, barstools, child seating, custom furniture -> /", "Six-step finishing process for table tops -> /quality", "Chairs and barstools built with hardwood frames, premium finishes, high