UPDATE companies SET description='Olmsted Automotive LLC operates from Hallam, Nebraska, serving as a specialist retailer and service provider for late-model muscle car parts and driveline conversions.

The company stocks and sells used OEM components for platforms including the C6 Corvette (2005–2013), Pontiac Firebird (1982–2002), Chevrolet Camaro (1982–2020), Cadillac CTS-V (2004–2020), Pontiac G8 (2008–2009), and Pontiac GTO (2004–2006). Inventory spans transmissions, torque-tube wiring harnesses, radiator fan assemblies, engine control modules, and bell housings. Beyond parts sales, Olmsted Automotive performs complete driveline swaps — documented projects include a 70 Nova LSA/TR6060 build at 842 RWHP, a 1979 Trans Am LS2/T56 swap, an 89 Camaro LS swap, a 1957 Chevrolet 3100 with a mystery motor, a C6 custom chassis at 996 HP, and a 1957 Chevy truck C6 hybrid conversion.

Customers range from individual enthusiasts restoring or upgrading muscle cars to shops seeking specific late-model drivetrain components. The company supports each platform with model-specific part listings and offers free VIN programming on ECMs.

Olmsted Automotive positions its driveline-swap expertise as its core differentiator, backing every swap combo with a 100% satisfaction guarantee, free ECM tuning, and an unlimited-mile limited warranty. The business emphasizes post-sale communication and support, citing customer feedback that highlights service responsiveness well over a year after purchase.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Driveline swap installation", "ECM tuning and VIN programming", "Used OEM parts sales", "Warranty administration", "Custom chassis fabrication"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Performance automotive", "Muscle car restoration"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Muscle car driveline swap specialization", "Free ECM tuning with swap purchases", "Unlimited-mile limited warranty on swaps", "100% satisfaction guarantee", "Late-model used OEM parts inventory for six GM platforms"], "facts_used": ["Location: Hallam, Nebraska -> db", "Platforms served: C6 Corvette, Pontiac Firebird, Chevrolet Camaro, Cadillac CTS-V, Pontiac G8, Pontiac GTO -> /", "Parts categories: transmissions, wiring harnesses, radiators, ECMs, bell housings -> /", "Swap projects documented: Nova, Trans Am, Camaro, 1957 Chevy truck, custom chassis -> /", "Guarantees: 100% satisfaction, free ECM tuning, unlimited-mile warranty -> /", "Customer testimonials referencing long-term support -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Your one stop shop for all late model used parts. Muscle Car Driveline Swap Specialists and Sales!", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='olmsted-automotive-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Olson Solar Energy operates from Onalaska, Wisconsin, with additional bases in La Crosse, Eau Claire, and Wausau, serving customers across Wisconsin, eastern Minnesota, and northern Iowa. The company was founded by twin brothers Cameron and Brandon Olson after they reunited in Wisconsin following years living in Washington state and North Carolina. Within months of their reunion, the pair launched the business as co‑owners, with Cameron serving as CEO and Brandon as COO. The venture grew from Brandon’s interest in solar energy sparked while living in the Pacific Northwest and Cameron’s background managing multi‑million‑dollar warehouses.

The firm specializes in designing and installing photovoltaic systems for residential and commercial clients. Its portfolio includes grid‑tied, hybrid, and off‑grid configurations, mounted on roofs or ground arrays. Project examples range from a 4‑kilowatt roof mount in La Crosse to a 21‑kilowatt roof mount in the same city, with installations documented from late 2019 through 2020. A commercial solar specialist and a design supervisor with a Building Science and Energy Management degree support the technical side, while two sales managers cover territories in Minnesota, Iowa, and southern and northeastern Wisconsin.

Customers are primarily homeowners and businesses seeking to reduce energy costs and carbon footprints. Installations have been completed in communities such as Onalaska, La Crosse, Mindoro, Viroqua, Green Bay, and Eau Claire. The company also works with referral partners and offers financing options to lower upfront barriers.

The founders emphasize a commitment to fast turnaround — aiming to complete every project in the shortest timeline possible — and a consultative approach that begins with a no‑cost evaluation using only an address and an energy bill. A referral program rewards existing customers, and the leadership cites a blend of work ethic, customer service, and passion for renewable energy as the foundation of their operation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system installation", "Grid\u2011tied system installation", "Hybrid system installation", "Off\u2011grid system installation", "Roof\u2011mount solar array installation", "Ground\u2011mount solar array installation", "Solar system design and engineering", "Free site evaluation and consultation", "Permitting and utility interconnection", "Commercial solar project development", "Residential solar project development", "Project management", "Sales and territory management", "Marketing and customer outreach"], "industries": ["Solar energy installation", "Renewable energy", "Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Energy efficiency"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Goal to complete every project in the shortest timeline possible", "Free solar evaluation with only an address and energy bill", "Referral program for existing customers", "Multiple Wisconsin locations (La Crosse, Eau Claire, Wausau) for regional coverage", "Offers grid\u2011tied, hybrid, and off\u2011grid system designs"], "facts_used": ["Operates from Onalaska, Wisconsin with bases in La Crosse, Eau Claire, Wausau -> /, /about-us", "Serves Wisconsin, eastern Minnesota, northern Iowa -> /, /about-us", "Founded by twin brothers Cameron and Brandon Olson -> /about-us", "Cameron Olson CEO, Brandon Olson COO, co-founders/co-owners -> /about-us", "Brandon inspired by Pacific Northwest, Cameron managed warehouses -> /about-us", "Specializes in gr