UPDATE companies SET description='Orbis Electric is headquartered in Santa Rosa, California. The company was founded by Marcus Hays, a U.S. Navy veteran and EV pioneer who set land-speed records on electric motorcycles, along with co-founders Chance Claxton and Scott Streeter. Hays began the venture with a vision to revolutionize electric propulsion through advanced axial-flux permanent-magnet motor technology, drawing on experience from the CALSTART Advanced Transportation Hatchery in Burbank.

The company develops axial-flux in-wheel motors (its Ring Drive Wheel) and the COOL•E platform, an intelligent power-recovery system for AI data centers that combines EV-derived drive technology, orchestrated controls, and predictive diagnostics across CDUs, pumps, fans, and chillers. Manufacturing capabilities include additive manufacturing, CNC machining, and casting. Orbis holds 16 issued patents and 40 pending applications, and collaborates with Ames National Laboratory and Oak Ridge National Laboratory on next-generation magnetic materials such as Cerium Gap and MAGMA technologies.

Orbis serves electric mobility (including a four-year validation program with Volkswagen Group in Germany), electric transport refrigeration (eTRU), defense propulsion, and AI data-center infrastructure. Its cooling platforms target megawatt-scale liquid cooling for 800 V DC-native architectures supporting next-generation AI compute, with customers referencing NVIDIA chip roadmaps.

The company states it was started to engineer more performance from less — born in electric mobility, proven in demanding applications, and reimagined for AI infrastructure. It positions its automotive- and defense-grade motor technology as a way to reduce cooling overhead, reclaim white space, protect uptime, and lessen dependence on critical mineral supply chains.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Axial-flux permanent-magnet motor design", "In-wheel motor development (Ring Drive Wheel)", "Liquid cooling system design", "Modular cooling system manufacturing", "Power electronics development", "Intelligent controls and predictive diagnostics", "Additive manufacturing", "CNC machining", "Casting", "Magnetic materials research (Cerium Gap, MAGMA)", "Megawatt-scale thermal management", "800 V DC power systems"], "industries": ["Electric vehicles / electric mobility", "Data centers / AI infrastructure", "Defense / military", "Transport refrigeration (eTRU)", "High-performance computing"], "materials": ["Magnetic materials (Cerium Gap, MAGMA technologies)", "Permanent magnets", "Critical minerals (supply-chain focus)"], "equipment": ["Additive manufacturing equipment", "CNC machines", "Casting equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["EV-derived drive technology applied to data-center cooling", "DC-native, power-agnostic platform (AC today, 800 V DC tomorrow)", "Automotive- and defense-grade motors for megawatt-scale liquid cooling", "16 issued patents and 40 pending applications", "Collaboration with Ames and Oak Ridge National Laboratories on magnetic materials"], "facts_used": ["HQ Santa Rosa, California -> db", "Founders Marcus Hays, Chance Claxton, Scott Streeter -> /about", "Marcus Hays US Navy veteran, EV pioneer, land speed records -> /about", "Axial-flux permanent-magnet motor technology, Ring Drive Wheel -> /about, /", "Four-year validation with Volkswagen Group Germany -> /about", "Applications: eTRU