UPDATE companies SET description='PC Plug Hawaii operates from a lab at 2290 Alahao Place in Honolulu’s Sand Island district. The company was founded by Liplop Tran, Eric Ligsay, and Ross Kanakuri, who shared a goal of delivering premium custom PC builds and straightforward repair services to the local community.

The shop specializes in custom PC assembly, component-level diagnostics, hardware repairs, and performance tuning. Services include full system builds with cable management and thermal optimization, SSD/RAM/GPU upgrades, operating system cleanup, phone and device repair (screen, battery, charging port), data recovery from SSDs and HDDs, password resets, and networking setup for home offices and small businesses. Walk-in service is available Monday through Saturday.

Customers range from gamers and content creators to students, home-office workers, streamers, and small businesses.

The founders started the business to offer a “luxury experience, zero attitude” — emphasizing transparent pricing, premium parts, clean aesthetics, and honest recommendations. They position the lab as a place where tech works flawlessly and looks premium doing it, with a focus on careful handling, privacy-first data handling, and clear communication throughout the process.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom PC building", "Budget planning and part selection", "Professional assembly and cable management", "Stress testing and thermal tuning", "System overclocking and BIOS optimization", "SSD/RAM/GPU/PSU/cooling upgrades", "OS cleanup and performance tuning", "Phone and device repair (screen, battery, charging port, speaker)", "Hardware diagnostics and thermal stability testing", "Password resets and account recovery (Windows/macOS)", "Secure settings review and backup setup", "Full re-wire and tidy cable routing", "Airflow optimization and RGB/controller cleanup", "PC troubleshooting (blue screens, no boot, random shutdowns)", "Device setup and optimization", "Upgrade roadmap guidance", "Quick how-to walkthroughs", "Data recovery (SSD/HDD assessment, backup, migration)", "Networking services (router/Wi-Fi optimization, hardwire/switch setup, security best practices)"], "industries": ["Gaming", "Content creation", "Education", "Small business", "Home office", "Streaming"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Varies by issue and parts availability; timeline provided after diagnostics", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Transparent pricing with premium parts and elite craftsmanship", "Showroom-ready cable management and clean build aesthetics", "Component-level diagnostics and transparent repair plans before spending", "Privacy-first data handling during recovery and repair", "Luxury service experience with zero attitude"], "facts_used": ["Location: 2290 Alahao Pl Unit #303A, Honolulu, HI 96819 -> /", "Owners: Liplop Tran, Eric Ligsay, Ross Kanakuri -> /about", "Founding goal: premium custom PC builds and honest tech repair -> /about", "Services: custom builds, repairs, upgrades, phone repair, data recovery, networking -> /services", "Customer types: gamers, creators, students, businesses, home offices, streamers -> /about, /services", "Differentiators: transparent pricing, premium parts, clean builds, luxury experience, privacy-first -> /about, /services", "Hours: Mon-Sat 10:00 AM - 6:00 PM -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''re a local Honolulu team specializing in custom PCs, upgrades, troubleshooting, and device repair.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pc-plug-hi/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pc-plug-hawaii' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pacific Die Cut Industries (PDCI) is headquartered in Lebanon, Kentucky. The company traces its origins to 1989 when it opened in the San Francisco Bay Area to address a shortage of custom automotive converting suppliers for Toyota and General Motors, offering just-in-time delivery and quality parts. No founders are named, and ownership structure is not disclosed.

PDCI converts non-rigid and thin rigid substrates into precision die-cut components through processes that include multi-station rotary die cutting, kiss cutting, lamination, slitting (up to 72 inches wide), CNC knife cutting, and clean-room manufacturing. The firm operates more than 4,000 square feet of Class 10,000 clean-room space with Class 1,000 capability, and provides value-added assembly, kitting, packaging, engineering support, and just-in-time logistics. Headcount and annual volume are not published.

The company serves four primary markets: automotive, where it acts as a Tier 1 and Tier 2 supplier of NVH gaskets, seals, and decorative interior trim to global OEMs; medical, producing clean-room components for wound care, diagnostic consumables, and wearable sensors; energy, converting photovoltaic films, adhesives, and conductive foils for solar and wind manufacturers; and electronics, laminating pressure-sensitive adhesives onto technical films, gaskets, and dielectric materials.

PDCI states its mission is to be the industry leader in custom conversion across medical, automotive, electronic, and industrial markets by delivering the highest quality in the shortest lead times. Its quality system emphasizes risk analysis (PFMEA), error-proofing (poka-yoke), and continuous improvement, supported by IATF 16949 and ISO 13485 certifications.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rotary Die Cutting", "Kiss Cutting", "Lamination", "Slitting (up to 72\")", "Clean Room Manufacturing (Class 10,000/1,000)", "CNC Knife Cutting", "Value-Added Assembly", "Engineering & Prototyping", "Packaging & Labeling", "Just-In-Time Logistics", "End-to-End Program Management"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical", "Energy", "Electronics", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Non-rigid substrates", "Thin rigid substrates", "Pressure-sensitive adhesives", "Photovoltaic films", "High-performance adhesives", "Surface protection masking", "Wire wrap", "Conductive foils", "Technical films", "Gasket materials", "Conductors", "Dielectric materials", "Medical-grade materials", "Chemically treated membranes", "Untreated membranes", "Glass microfibers", "High-modulus foams", "Fabric-backed foams"], "equipment": ["Multi-station rotary die cutting systems", "High-speed kiss cutting presses with ultra-sensitive optics", "Computerized single-lever slitting equipment", "Score slitting equipment", "Shear slitting equipment", "CNC knife cutting systems", "Computer-aided nesting software"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Just-in-time logistics with daily, weekly, and Kanban releases", "Over 4,000 sq ft Class 10,000 clean room with Class 1,000 availability", "Multi-station computer-controlled rotary die cutting with ultra-sensitive optics for accurate registration", "End-to-end manufacturing from conceptualization through distribution", "Advanced slitting capabilities up to 72\" width including shear slitting of chemically treated membranes"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Lebanon, Kentucky -> db", "Founded 1989 in Bay Area to serve Toyota and GM -> /about", "Tier 1 & 2 automotive supplier of die cut NVH, gaskets, seals, trim -> /", "Medical clean room manufacturing for wound care, diagnostics, wearables -> /", "Energy market: conversion of photovoltaic films, adhesives, conductive foils -> /", "Electronics: lamination of pressure sensitive adhesives on technical films -> /", "Clean room: over 4,000 sq ft Class 10,000 with Class 1,000 availability -> /capabilities", "Processes: rotary die cutting, kiss cutting, lamination, slitting up to 72\", CNC knife cutting, value-add assembly, engineering, packaging, JIT logistics, end-to-end manufacturing -> /capabilities", "Certifications: IATF 16949:2016 (California, Kentucky), ISO 13485:2016 (California) -> /quality", "Quality methods: PFMEA, poka-yoke, APQP, PPAP, FAIR -> /quality", "Mission: industry leader in custom conversion across medical, automotive, electronic, industrial -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PDCI Automotive is a Tier 1 & 2 supplier of die cut NVH, extruded and laminated gaskets, seals, and decorative interior trim components to top global automotive OEMs.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pdci-automotive' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PDQ South operates from Pageland, South Carolina, where it has been in business for over 42 years. The company, known as PDQ South Technologies, was built on the principles of Pride, Determination, and Quality, though its founding year and original founders are not publicly documented.

The shop specializes in contract manufacturing, custom injection molding, and precision machining. Its injection molding presses range up to 550 tons, supported by in-house mold making, design, and repair capabilities. The machining department runs CNC milling up to 5-axis, CNC turning, EDM, and manual mill and lathe work, all programmed through CAD/CAM systems including SolidWorks, SolidCam, DP Esprit, and Surfcam. A recently completed state-of-the-art manufacturing plant houses the tooling and machining departments, expanding capacity for both molding and machining work. Value-added services such as pad printing, hot stamping, and assembly are also offered.

Specific industry sectors are not detailed in available materials, but the company''s capabilities target applications needing integrated tooling and production under one roof.

The company emphasizes that its in-house tooling and design eliminate the need for outside vendors, shortening lead times and optimizing part cost, quality, and performance. Its name reflects a philosophy of exceeding customer expectations through integrated mold building, molding, and machining services.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (up to 550 tons)", "Mold making", "Mold design", "Mold repair", "CNC milling (up to 5-axis)", "CNC turning", "EDM machining", "Manual milling", "Manual turning", "CAD/CAM programming (SolidWorks, SolidCam, DP Esprit, Surfcam)", "Custom machining", "Production machining", "Pad printing", "Hot stamping", "Assembly"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house mold making, design, and repair for faster turnaround", "Injection molding capacity up to 550 tons", "CNC machining including 5-axis milling, turning, and EDM", "Integrated CAD/CAM with SolidWorks, SolidCam, DP Esprit, and Surfcam", "Value-added services: pad printing, hot stamping, assembly"], "facts_used": ["Location: Pageland, South Carolina -> db", "Over 42 years in business -> /about", "In-house mold making, design, and repair -> /about", "Injection molding up to 550 tons -> /about", "CAD/CAM with SolidWorks, SolidCam, DP Esprit, Surfcam -> /about", "CNC milling up to 5-axis, CNC lathe, EDM machining, manual milling and lathe -> /about", "Value-added services: pad printing, hot stamping, assembly -> /about", "New state-of-the-art manufacturing plant housing tooling and machining departments -> /about", "Contract manufacturing, custom injection molding, mold making, design, repair, CNC machining, general tool shop functions -> /about", "PDQ Difference: Pride, Determination, Quality -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our specialties encompass contract manufacturing, custom injection molding including mold making, design, and repair, as well as CNC machining and all general tool shop functions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pdq-south' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PFC Furniture Industries, Inc. operates as a wholesale furniture distributor from its headquarters in Richardson, Texas, within the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex. The company supplies independent furniture retailers across Texas and most of Oklahoma with a range of home furnishings.

The distributor carries living room, bedroom, dining, bedding, and a custom rustic farmhouse collection, along with close-out and special-deal inventories that are offered to dealer accounts. PFC does not sell directly to consumers; instead, it refers retail shoppers to local dealer partners through a referral system.

Its customer base consists of independent furniture retailers in Texas and Oklahoma. The company provides dealer-only access to wholesale pricing and product selections through a login portal, and it runs weekly featured specials and monthly promotions for its dealer network. The business focuses on the independent retail channel, offering a curated mix of stocked and close-out furniture lines.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale furniture distribution", "Dealer account management", "Product sourcing and curation", "Close-out inventory management", "Consumer dealer referral"], "industries": ["Furniture retail", "Home furnishings", "Independent retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dealer-only wholesale pricing with online account portal", "Service area covering Texas and most of Oklahoma", "Consumer referral program to local dealers", "Weekly featured specials and monthly promotions for dealers", "Close-out and discount inventory management"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Richardson, Texas -> db", "Wholesale furniture distributor -> homepage", "Serves independent furniture retailers in Texas and most of Oklahoma -> homepage", "Product categories: living room, bedroom, dining, bedding, custom rustic farmhouse -> homepage", "Dealer-only wholesale pricing with login portal -> homepage", "Consumer referral program to local dealers -> homepage", "Weekly featured specials and monthly promotions -> homepage", "Close-out and discount inventory management -> homepage"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "PFC Furniture Industries serves independent furniture retailers throughout Texas and most of Oklahoma with living room, bedroom, dining, bedding and other home furnishings.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownershi