UPDATE companies SET description='PFI, a member of the Grote Company Family of Brands, is headquartered in San Antonio, Texas, with manufacturing operations in Algona, Iowa. The business traces its roots back more than 60 years to the KOFAB and Meyer Industries lines, which were later unified under the PFI name. Today it operates as a family-owned enterprise led by CEO Bob Grote and COO Jack Grote, part of a multi-brand group that emphasizes shared engineering and support resources.

The company designs and builds sanitary, custom-configured conveying and handling equipment for food processors. Its product lineup includes belt conveyors, bucket and incline conveyors, dumpers, horizontal motion conveyors, and vibratory conveyors and feeders. In addition to equipment manufacturing, PFI provides in-house installation, technical service, replacement parts such as belts, buckets, pulleys, and stainless-steel hydraulic cylinders, and maintenance training. The firm serves customers from two locations, integrating systems with other OEMs to deliver complete line solutions.

PFI serves a broad range of food sectors, including bakery, candy and confectionery, cereal, dairy, frozen foods, fruits and vegetables, meat, poultry and seafood, nuts, pasta, pet food, ready-to-eat meals, and snack foods. Reference customers cited by the company include Hormel, a bakery processor, a snacks processor, and a large food processor, as well as Grillo''s Pickles, which expanded production using integrated solutions from the Grote family of brands.

PFI says its differentiation rests on five pillars: dependable solutions built for long-term viability, integration-ready designs that fit existing lines, sanitary construction that meets or exceeds regulations, a collaborative approach with customer teams and other OEMs, and a customer commitment that spans pre-project planning through post-installation support. Leadership attributes the company''s culture to its family-run heritage, noting that the partnership with the Grote group was driven by aligned values as much as by capability fit.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sanitary conveying equipment manufacturing", "Custom configuration", "System integration", "In-house installation", "Technical service", "Parts supply", "Maintenance training", "Line integration project management", "Belt conveying", "Bucket & incline conveying", "Dumping", "Horizontal motion conveying", "Vibratory conveying & feeding", "Conveyor belt replacement", "Elevator bucket replacement", "Pulley replacement", "Stainless steel hydraulic cylinder supply"], "industries": ["Bakery", "Candy & Confectionery", "Cereal", "Dairy", "Frozen Food", "Fruits & Vegetables", "Meat, Poultry, & Seafood", "Nuts", "Pasta", "Pet Food", "Ready-To-Eat", "Snack Food"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Belt Conveyors", "Bucket & Incline Conveyors", "Dumpers", "Horizontal Motion Conveyors", "Vibratory Conveyors & Feeders", "Conveyor Belts", "Elevator Buckets", "Pulleys", "Stainless Steel Hydraulic Cylinders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dependable solutions built for long-term viability", "Integration-ready designs that fit existing lines", "Sanitary construction meeting or exceeding regulations", "Collaborative approach with customer teams and other OEMs", "Customer commitment from planning through post-installation support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters San Antonio, Texas -> db", "Manufacturing location Algona, Iowa -> /about", "Over 60 years experience, started as KOFAB and Meyer Industries -> /about", "Family-owned, led by Bob Grote (CEO) and Jack Grote (COO) -> /about", "Manufactures sanitary custom-configured conveying solutions -> /about", "Equipment categories: belt, bucket & incline, dumpers, horizontal motion, vibratory conveyors & feeders -> /", "Services: in-house installation, technical service, parts supply, maintenance training -> /, /about", "Industries served: bakery, candy, cereal, dairy, frozen, fruits/veg, meat/poultry/seafood, nuts, pasta, pet food, ready-to-eat, snack -> /", "Customer examples: Hormel, bakery processor, snacks processor, large food processor, Grillo''s Pickles -> /, /about", "Differentiators: dependable, integration-ready, sanitary designs, collaborative, customer commitment -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "WE MANUFACTURE SANITARY, CUSTOM-CONFIGURED CONVEYING SOLUTIONS FOR THE FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRY", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pficonveyors/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pfi' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PFI Inc. operates from Longwood, Florida, as a distributor of surface-mount technology (SMT) and printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) equipment. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm supplies a broad range of equipment categories including pick-and-place machines, automated optical inspection (AOI) and solder paste inspection (SPI) systems, aqueous and batch cleaning systems, conformal coating equipment, reflow ovens, wave and selective soldering machines, depaneling routers, screen printers, and test equipment such as in-circuit and flying-probe testers. It also stocks feeder carts and feeders for major placement platforms from Myronic, Juki, Europlacer, Panasonic, Fuji, ASM, Universal Instruments, and Yamaha. In addition to equipment sales, PFI maintains an in-house service technician team and a logistics department that coordinates shipping.

The inventory includes both new and used units, such as a 2023 Aqueous Technologies Trident ZDO cleaner, a 2023 Essemtec PUMA2 pick-and-place system with feeder package, a 2016 OSAI Automation Neo router with dust extraction and chiller, and 2017–2018 Electrovert/ITW Aquastorm inline and batch washers.

The company emphasizes its in-house technical support and logistics capabilities as differentiators, offering economical shipping options and secure payment via major credit cards and PayPal.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SMT/PCBA equipment distribution", "In-house equipment service and support", "Conformal coating equipment supply", "Logistics and shipping coordination"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Electrovert/ITW Aquastorm 100C InLine Wash", "Electrovert/ITW Aquastorm 50 Batch Cleaner", "Aqueous Technologies Trident ZDO", "Essemtec PUMA2-PPD-C & Feeder Package", "OSAI Automation Neo Router w/BOFA Dust Extractor & Thermo Chiller", "Myronic/Mydata feeders", "Juki feeders", "Europlacer feeders & carts", "Panasonic feeders", "Fuji NXT/AIMEX feeders", "ASM/Siplace feeders", "Universal Precision Pro feeders", "Yamaha/Assembleon feeders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house service technicians for equipment support", "In-house logistics department with economical shipping options", "Secure payment acceptance (major credit cards, PayPal)", "Broad multi-brand inventory covering major SMT equipment platforms"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location from db", "Equipment categories and specific machine listings from /", "In-house service technicians and logistics from /", "Payment methods from /", "Feeder brands from /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "PFI Inc. - SMT / PCBA Equipment ... Sale price $ 0.00", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pfi-inc-pcba-electronic-assembly-equipment' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PGT Energy Solutions operates from Phoenix, Arizona, serving homeowners and businesses across the state with solar and battery storage installations. The company does not publish a founding year, though it advertises more than 25 years of industry experience.

The firm installs residential and commercial photovoltaic systems and integrates battery storage, including Tesla Powerwall units, to enable grid-charged load shifting. Its core service is designing systems that charge during off-peak utility hours and discharge during peak periods, reducing demand charges from Arizona utilities such as APS and SRP. The company also provides zero-down financing options and warranty support for installed systems.

Primary customers are Arizona homeowners seeking lower electricity bills and backup power, as well as commercial clients aiming to cut demand charges. The company works directly with rate structures from Arizona Public Service (APS) and Salt River Project (SRP), tailoring battery configurations to each utility’s time-of-use and demand-based plans.

PGT Energy Solutions differentiates itself through NABCEP-certified installers, an Arizona-based team, BBB accreditation, and status as an Arizona Local Certified Energy Partner. It emphasizes the 30% federal investment tax credit and state rebates for standalone battery installations, positioning its offerings as a way to achieve energy independence without requiring rooftop solar.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certified','BBB Accredited','Arizona Local Certified Energy Partner']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Battery storage installation", "Grid-charged battery system design", "Load shifting for time-of-use rates", "Demand charge reduction", "Time-of-use rate optimization", "Backup power system installation", "Tesla Powerwall installation", "Energy storage system design"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Battery storage", "Energy storage"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["25+ years industry experience", "NABCEP-certified installers", "Arizona-based installation team", "Zero-down financing options", "BBB accredited business"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "25+ years experience claimed -> /about-us", "NABCEP Certified -> /about-us", "BBB Accredited -> /", "Arizona Local Certified Energy Partner -> /", "Offers residential solar, commercial solar, battery storage installation -> /about-us", "Installs Tesla Powerwall -> /about-us", "Provides zero-down financing and warranty support -> /about-us", "Serves APS and SRP utility customers -> /about-us", "Contact: Tempe, AZ 85283, ,  -> /about-us", "Social media: Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "At PGT Energy Solutions, we help Arizona homeowners take control of their energy costs with advanced home battery systems designed for APS peak rates and SRP demand charges.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pgt-energy-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PHT Systems, headquartered in New Brighton, Minnesota, was founded in 1981 as a distributor of Henny Penny pressure fryers. In December 2018, Chris Reichert acquired the company and serves as president, steering its expansion across the Midwest and Southern California.

The company operates as a national wholesale distributor of foodservice equipment, breadings, seasonings, and supplies from manufacturers. It holds exclusive distribution rights for Henny Penny in the Midwest and Southern California and maintains an extensive parts inventory supported by a fleet of service trucks. PHT also provides consulting, on-site training, and equipment service and repair, with technicians available 24/7.

PHT serves the foodservice, retail, and hospitality sectors, supplying supermarkets, convenience stores, restaurants, universities, and other hospitality locations. It also partners with dealers who resell equipment and training services. Longtime customers include JL Beers, Boelter Premier, and fresh-food operations that rely on PHT for equipment uptime and staff training.

The company emphasizes a "whatever it takes" philosophy, focusing on customer support beyond the sale. Its differentiators include a no-charge return-trip policy if a needed part is not on the service truck, extensive hands-on training programs led by a dedicated training director, and a service team with decades of combined experience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Equipment distribution", "Customer training and retraining", "Equipment service and repair", "Parts supply and inventory management", "Consulting for foodservice operations", "Breading and seasoning program development"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Retail", "Hospitality"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Henny Penny pressure fryers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exclusive distributor for Henny Penny in the Midwest and Southern California", "No-charge return trip if part not on service truck", "24/7 expert technician support", "Dedicated customer training and retraining programs", "Consulting, service, and repair beyond equipment sales"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 in Minnesota -> /about", "Chris Reichert purchased company December 2018 -> /about", "Headquarters New Brighton, Minnesota -> db", "Exclusive distributor for Henny Penny in Midwest and Southern California -> /about, /", "National wholesale distributor of foodservice equipment, breadings, seasonings, supplies -> /about", "Extensive parts inventory, service trucks, 24/7 support -> /, /about", "Customer training and retraining programs -> /, /about", "Service and repair, consulting -> /about", "Industries served: retail, foodservice, hospitality -> /", "Customer testimonials: JL Beers, Boelter Premier -> /", "No-charge return trip policy -> /", "Team members and tenures -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "PHT is a national wholesale distributor of foodservice equipment, breadings and seasonings, and supplies from leading manufacturers.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pht-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PMC SMART Solutions traces its roots to 1929, when two families founded Plastic Moldings Company in Cincinnati, Ohio, during the Great Depression. The business relocated to Shelbyville, Indiana, and remains privately owned by the founding family. President and CEO Lisa Jennings leads the fourth generation of family ownership; the company earned WBE and WOSB certification in 2013.

The firm specializes in complex engineering and technical solutions for difficult-to-mold, high-temperature components. Its core capabilities include high-temperature and implantable biomaterials injection molding, hyper-precision molding and insert molding to micron tolerances, scientific injection molding, insert and over-molding, and complete secondary operations and assembly. PMC also provides design and engineering services, technology development, and quality systems management.

PMC serves the medical device and automotive industries. It is a strategic supplier to Medtronic and has worked with Bosch Automotive. The company’s components are used in life-saving medical technologies and high-performance automotive applications.

