UPDATE companies SET description='Pacific Industrial Equipment operates from Waipahu, Hawaii, serving customers across the Hawaiian Islands and Guam. The business functions as a division of Industrial Vacuum Equipment Corporation, a Wisconsin-based company with a long history in industrial vacuum and blasting applications. No founding date or individual founders are disclosed in public materials.

Its Waipahu facility stocks replacement parts, accessories, and consumables for immediate availability. Equipment offerings include cartridge and baghouse dust collectors, 2‑stage digital air compressors (50–400 hp), diesel and electric vacuums, Sponge Jet™ low‑dust blasting systems, and portable dehumidifiers. Pacific Industrial also supplies on‑site operator training and supports both short‑ and long‑term rental agreements.

Primary customers include shipyards, bridge and tank painting contractors, refineries, environmental remediation firms, and general construction companies. The equipment is also used in asbestos abatement, roofing, abrasive blast recovery, hazardous waste removal, carbon removal, steel mill maintenance, and flood‑damage drying. The Hawaii location supports projects throughout the Pacific region, including Guam.

